      "audio": {
        "slotId": "narration-main",
        "text": "For one week, America closed every bank."
      },
      "caption": "THE WEEK AMERICA CLOSED EVERY BANK",
      "evidenceSourceIds": ["loc-bank-run-1931"]
    },
    {
      "id": "panic",
      "startFrame": 150,
      "endFrame": 420,
      "visual": {
        "kind": "archival-image",
        "sourceId": "loc-bank-run-1931",
        "motion": "pan-left"
      },
      "audio": {
        "slotId": "narration-main",
        "text": "By March 1933, fear had become a financial force. Depositors rushed for cash, and banks failed faster than confidence could recover."
      },
      "caption": "MARCH 1933",
      "evidenceSourceIds": ["loc-bank-run-1931", "loc-bank-holiday-context"]
    },
    {
      "id": "bank-holiday",
      "startFrame": 420,
      "endFrame": 720,
      "visual": {
        "kind": "typographic-card",
        "headline": "A NATIONAL BANK HOLIDAY",
        "motion": "paper-reveal"
      },
      "audio": {
        "slotId": "narration-main",
        "text": "Roosevelt answered with a national bank holiday: stop the withdrawals, inspect the banks, and reopen only those judged sound."
      },
      "caption": "MARCH 6, 1933",
      "evidenceSourceIds": ["loc-bank-holiday-context"]
    },
    {
      "id": "trust-problem",
      "startFrame": 720,
      "endFrame": 1020,
      "visual": {
        "kind": "archival-image",
        "sourceId": "loc-bank-run-1931",
        "motion": "slow-pull-out"
      },
      "audio": {
        "slotId": "narration-main",
        "text": "The machinery mattered. But the deeper crisis was human: a banking system works only while people believe their money will be there."
      },
      "caption": "THE REAL CRISIS WAS CONFIDENCE",
      "evidenceSourceIds": ["fdr-fireside-transcript-1933-03-12"]
    },
    {
      "id": "radio-setup",
      "startFrame": 1020,
      "endFrame": 1380,
      "visual": {
        "kind": "archival-image",
        "sourceId": "nara-fdr-fireside-photo-1933-03-12",
        "motion": "slow-push-in"
      },
      "audio": {
        "slotId": "narration-main",
        "text": "On March 12, Roosevelt entered American homes by radio and asked the public to become part of the rescue."
      },
      "caption": "MARCH 12, 1933 — THE FIRST FIRESIDE CHAT",
      "evidenceSourceIds": [
        "nara-fdr-fireside-photo-1933-03-12",
        "fdr-fireside-transcript-1933-03-12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "archival-voice",
      "startFrame": 1380,
      "endFrame": 1740,
      "visual": {
        "kind": "archival-image",
        "sourceId": "nara-fdr-fireside-photo-1933-03-12",
        "motion": "hold-with-film-grain"
      },
      "audio": {
        "slotId": "fdr-archival-excerpt",
        "sourceInMs": 736000,
        "sourceOutMs": 748000,
        "transcript": "After all, there is an element in the readjustment of our financial system more important than currency, more important than gold, and that is the confidence of the people themselves."
      },
      "caption": "\u201cTHE CONFIDENCE OF THE PEOPLE THEMSELVES\u201d",
      "evidenceSourceIds": [
        "fdr-fireside-audio-1933-03-12",
        "fdr-fireside-transcript-1933-03-12"
      ]
